---
/**
 * The pitch: why to try olai, and pictures of what a person sees. How to do
 * a thing belongs on a docs page; each section here ends with a link to it.
 */
import { markdownToHtml } from "satteri"

import { DEFAULT_THEME, PALETTES } from "../../../packages/appearance/src/palettes.ts"
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import { siteMap } from "../sitemap.ts"
import "../styles/home.css"

// Every plugin olai ships, as the docs index lists them (a test holds the
// index to the registry), so this list cannot fall behind the build.
const plugins = (await siteMap()).groups.find((group) => group.title === "Plugins")
if (plugins === undefined) throw new Error('docs/index.md has no "## Plugins" group')

// The plugin pitch, with its side facts as footnotes, written the way a docs
// page writes them so the same renderer draws markers and notes alike. The
// notes go to the foot of the page.
const { html } = markdownToHtml(
  `**Ask for one.** Press ⌘K, say in one sentence what it should do, and an agent writes it while you watch.[^agenda] Read what it does, press **Turn on**, and it starts drawing in the page you are on. No reload, no install, no build.[^folder] Your settings travel with your notes.[^settings]

[^agenda]: The worked example is a morning agenda: from 7 in the morning it sends the rows that are overdue or due today into each node agent's conversation, once a day. [Read the morning agenda](/docs/dynamic-plugins-examples/#the-morning-agenda).

[^folder]: What you are left with is a folder in your own directory: a README anybody can read, and the code. Git records every line of it. Copy the folder into another directory and it arrives switched off, until a person there turns it on.

[^settings]: A plugin you asked for keeps its settings in the same file as the plugins olai ships. A top-level row in \`_olai/Settings.olai\` names each plugin; its properties choose how it behaves and whether it runs. The **Plugins** panel writes the same file. See the [settings docs](/docs/settings/).
`,
  { features: { gfm: true } },
)
const [pitch = "", notes = ""] = html.split(/(?=<section data-footnotes)/)
---

<Base
  title="olai: notes and to-do lists in plain files, with the AI agent you choose"
  description="olai is an open-source outliner that you run on your own computer. You write items and mark them done. An AI agent that you choose can edit them with you."
>
<main>

<div class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="kicker">open source · plain files · the AI agent you choose</p>
        <div class="brand">
          <h1>olai</h1>
          <img class="leafmark" src="/leaf.jpg" width="1024" height="1365" alt="A palm leaf drawn in ink, with coral tips. It is the olai mark.">
        </div>
        <p class="tag">Notes and to-do lists that you and an AI agent edit together.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-say">
        <p class="sub">olai is an outliner. An outline is a list of items, and an
        item can hold more items under it. You write items, mark them done, and
        give them dates. An AI agent does the same when you ask it. olai saves
        your work as plain files on your own computer.</p>
        <p class="next">
          <a href="#try">What you need to run olai</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="shot crop">
      <img src="/tour/outline-and-chat.png" width="2880" height="1800" alt="olai in a browser. The sidebar on the left lists two outlines. The middle shows the outline Kitchen renovation, with six of seven items marked done. The right shows a chat in which an agent marks items done.">
    </figure>
    <p class="caption only-wide">The real app. The middle pane shows an outline. The right pane shows a chat with an agent about that outline. The agent has marked four items done. The agent in this picture is scripted, so that the picture can be made again when olai changes.</p>
    <p class="caption only-narrow">A close view of the real app. An agent has marked four items of this outline done. The agent in this picture is scripted.</p>

    <ul class="points three">
      <li><b>Your notes are plain files.</b>
        <span>olai keeps them in a directory, which is a folder on your computer. An outline is a text file with one item per line, written as JSON. A document is a Markdown file. If you stop using olai, the files stay where they are.</span></li>
      <li><b>You choose the AI agent.</b>
        <span>olai has no AI of its own. It runs Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Pi, or Oh My Pi with the account that you already have. You pick the agent each time you start a chat.</span></li>
      <li><b>You see every change.</b>
        <span>The agent works in a chat beside the outline. Each change appears on the page when the agent makes it. olai records your changes and the agent's changes in git, so you can read them later.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="honest"><b>What it takes today.</b> olai is new. It runs on a Mac or a Linux computer, and you start it from a terminal with Nix. olai has no phone app and no account to create. Read <a href="#try">what you need to run olai</a>.</p>

    <nav class="chapters" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#agent">AI agents</a>
      <a href="#compare">comparison</a>
      <a href="#agenda">what is due</a>
      <a href="#find">filter and search</a>
      <a href="#plugins">plugins</a>
      <a href="#try">run olai</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="compare">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Compared to Workflowy and Dynalist</h2>
    <p class="lead">Same outlining model — indent, move, mirror, check off.
    The difference is where the data lives.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table class="cmp">
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>Workflowy, Dynalist</th><th>olai</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Storage</td><td>A hosted database</td><td>Plain files in a directory you choose</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sync</td><td>Their cloud</td><td>git, or anything that moves files</td></tr>
          <tr><td>History</td><td>In-app version history</td><td>git log</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Search</td><td>Keyword, in their app</td><td>Filter the page you’re on, or search the whole directory</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Source</td><td>Proprietary</td><td><a href="https://github.com/juspay/olai">Open source</a> (AGPL-3.0)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Outlines are ordinary files. The
    <a href="/docs/format/">format spec</a>
    is there if you want it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="agenda">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What’s due</h2>
    <p class="lead">Dated work from every outline, on one page. Late things
    sit above today. A birthday isn’t a task — it stays on its day and never
    turns red. The calendar is a
    <a href="#plugins">plugin</a>.</p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="file">/agenda · 2026-08-12</div>

        <div class="spine">
          <span class="line"></span>

          <div class="day gone">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <p class="dayname">5 days ago · Fri, Aug 7</p>
            <div class="row"><span class="box doing"></span><span class="t">Order the new cabinets <span class="tagchip">#blocking</span></span><span class="pill late">5 days late</span></div>
            <p class="trail">Kitchen renovation</p>
          </div>

          <div class="day now">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <p class="dayname"><span class="lead">Today</span> · Wed, Aug 12</p>
            <div class="row"><span class="box"></span><span class="t">Book the plumber</span></div>
            <p class="trail">Kitchen renovation</p>
          </div>

          <div class="day near">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <p class="dayname">Sat, Aug 15<span class="away">in 3 days</span></p>
            <div class="row"><span class="box"></span><span class="t">Template the countertop</span></div>
            <p class="trail">Kitchen renovation</p>
          </div>

          <p class="quiet short">two quiet weeks</p>

          <div class="day far">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <p class="dayname">Fri, Aug 28<span class="away">in 2 weeks</span></p>
            <div class="row"><span class="box"></span><span class="t">Meet the tiler on site</span><span class="pill">14:00</span></div>
            <p class="trail">Kitchen renovation</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>A file named for the day — 2026-08-12.md, anywhere in
        the directory — is that day’s note. Open the day and the note is on
        top, with everything dated that day underneath it.</p>
        <p>Weekly chores come back as a fresh row on the next date, so eleven
        Mondays are eleven rows, not one row whose date kept moving.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="find">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Filter the page you are on</h2>
    <p class="lead">Type in the box above the outline and the rows that don’t
    match are hidden. Clicking a tag does the same. The query is in the page’s
    address, so you can send the filtered page to someone as a link.</p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="file">/house.olai?q=%23home+OR+alcove</div>
        <div class="row"><span class="bullet">●</span><span class="t"><strong>kitchen remodel</strong> <span class="tagchip"><span class="hit">#home</span></span></span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="bullet">●</span><span class="t">order the new cabinets</span></div>
        <div class="noteline">…measure the <span class="hit">alcove</span> before ordering.</div>
        <div class="row d1 dimrow"><span class="bullet">●</span><span class="t">install the cabinets</span></div>
        <div class="row d2"><span class="box"></span><span class="t">pick the hinges <span class="tagchip"><span class="hit">#home</span></span></span></div>
        <p class="caption">Matches stay where they live. Ancestors stay so a
        bare title still makes sense.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Done, last week, a quoted phrase — the rest of the query language
        is in the
        <a href="/docs/search/">search docs</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="type">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Type like an outliner</h2>
    <p class="lead">Click a title to edit it in place. Enter makes the next
    line. Tab indents. The rest is the usual outliner muscle memory.</p>
    <div class="cols">
      <table class="keys">
        <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>commit, and open the next line</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> mid-line</td><td>split the row in two, there</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Backspace</kbd> at the start</td><td>join this row onto the one above</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>indent, or out again</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>↑</kbd>/<kbd>↓</kbd></td><td>move a row among its siblings</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>Z</kbd></td><td>take back your last edit here</td></tr>
      </table>
      <table class="keys">
        <tr><td><kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>tick it off, or take that back</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>⇧</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>walk the mark on: to do, then doing, then none</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>⇧</kbd>+<kbd>D</kbd></td><td>duplicate the row, and everything under it</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>⇧</kbd>+<kbd>M</kbd></td><td>move it under a row you search for, anywhere</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>write the note under it</td></tr>
        <tr><td><kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>drop what you were typing</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Off a Mac, ⌘ is Ctrl. The full map — dragging, the
    palette, pins, the inbox — is in the
    <a href="/docs/editing/">editing docs</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="prefs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>How it looks</h2>
    <p class="lead">Four palettes — two by day, two by night — and an unpicked page follows your OS. Press a chip; this page follows.</p>
    <div class="chips" role="list">
      {PALETTES.map((palette) => (
        <span class:list={["chip", { on: palette.name === DEFAULT_THEME }]} data-theme={palette.name} role="listitem">{palette.name}</span>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="cols">
      <div class="panel" data-theme="basalt">
        <div class="file">kitchen.olai · basalt</div>
        <div class="row"><span class="bullet">●</span><span class="t"><strong>Kitchen renovation</strong> <span class="rollup">2/4</span></span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box done"></span><span class="t strike">Demolition</span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box doing"></span><span class="t">Order the new cabinets <span class="tagchip">#blocking</span></span><span class="pill late">2026-08-07</span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box"></span><span class="t">Book the plumber</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" data-theme="reef">
        <div class="file">kitchen.olai · reef</div>
        <div class="row"><span class="bullet">●</span><span class="t"><strong>Kitchen renovation</strong> <span class="rollup">2/4</span></span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box done"></span><span class="t strike">Demolition</span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box doing"></span><span class="t">Order the new cabinets <span class="tagchip">#blocking</span></span><span class="pill late">2026-08-07</span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box"></span><span class="t">Book the plumber</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="agent">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>A coding agent edits your outlines with you</h2>
    <p class="lead">A chat opens on the row it is about, beside that row’s
    page. You keep typing while it works. It ticks off tasks and rewrites
    Markdown files, and you watch the page change. Git records both of you.</p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div class="panel chat">
        <div class="file">chat</div>
        <div class="ctx"><span>◦</span><span>Book the plumber</span></div>
        <div class="msg you">plumber's booked — tick it off</div>
        <div class="op"><b>✓</b> marked done · Book the plumber</div>
        <div class="wrote"><span>✓</span><span>Book the plumber</span><span class="said">Done</span></div>
        <div class="in">kitchen.olai</div>
        <div class="msg agent">Done. Marked “Book the plumber” as done.</div>

        <div class="msg you">the base units are carcass-only — say so in the doc</div>
        <div class="op"><b>✓</b> cabinets.md</div>
        <div class="fdiff">
          <p class="path"><span class="name">cabinets.md</span><span class="plus">+3</span><span class="minus">−2</span></p>
          <div class="body">
            <div class="ln"><span class="no">1</span><span class="mk">&nbsp;</span><span class="src"># Cabinet specs</span></div>
            <div class="ln gap"><span class="no"></span><span class="src">⋯ 3 unchanged</span></div>
            <div class="ln del"><span class="no">6</span><span class="mk">-</span><span class="src">- 600&#8239;mm base × 4</span></div>
            <div class="ln add"><span class="no">6</span><span class="mk">+</span><span class="src">- 600&#8239;mm base × 4, carcass only</span></div>
            <div class="ln add"><span class="no">7</span><span class="mk">+</span><span class="src">- filler strip × 2</span></div>
            <div class="ln"><span class="no">8</span><span class="mk">&nbsp;</span><span class="src">- corner carousel × 1</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="more">+4 more lines</p>
        </div>
        <div class="msg agent">Added the carcass note and the filler strips.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="file">kitchen.olai · live</div>
        <div class="row"><span class="bullet">●</span><span class="t"><strong>Kitchen renovation</strong> <span class="rollup">3/4</span></span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box doing"></span><span class="t">Order the new cabinets <span class="tagchip">#blocking</span></span></div>
        <div class="row d1"><span class="box done"></span><span class="t strike">Book the plumber</span></div>
        <p class="caption">The page updates because the file on disk
        changed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">How to point an agent at a running olai is in the
    <a href="/docs/chat/">chat docs</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="plugins">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Plugins</h2>
    <p class="lead">The outline editor, the Markdown reader, the shell, chat,
    git, search — they are plugins. They show on one panel. Switch one off
    while olai is running; the rest keep going. The runtime is
    <a href="https://github.com/cordiverse/cordis">Cordis</a>, a meta-framework
    of spatiotemporal composability. The paper is on
    <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25512" title="A Programming Paradigm for Spatiotemporal Composability">arXiv</a>.</p>
    <div class="plugmock" aria-label="The plugins panel: one line per plugin, grouped, each with its switch">
      <div class="plughead"><strong>Plugins</strong><a href="/docs/settings/">Settings.olai ↗</a></div>
      <div class="plugbody">
<details class="pluggroup plugneeds" open><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Needs attention</span><span>1</span></summary>
<div class="plugrow plugopen"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Mail</span><span class="plugstate">Needs setup</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable mail"></span></div>
<div class="plugdetail">No Gmail account connected.<br><button type="button" tabindex="-1">Connect Gmail</button></div>
</details>
<details class="pluggroup" open><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Agents</span><span>4 on · 2 off</span></summary>
<div class="plugrow"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Chat</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable chat"></span></div>
<div class="plugrow"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Claude Code</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable claude"></span></div>
<div class="plugrow"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Codex</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable codex"></span></div>
<div class="plugrow"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">OpenCode</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable opencode"></span></div>
<div class="plugrow plugoff"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Pi</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable pi"></span></div>
<div class="plugrow plugoff"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Oh My Pi</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable omp"></span></div>
</details>
<details class="pluggroup"><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Notes</span><span>19 on</span></summary></details>
<details class="pluggroup"><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Connections</span><span>6 on · 1 off</span></summary></details>
<details class="pluggroup"><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Interface</span><span>10 on</span></summary></details>
<details class="pluggroup" open><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Your plugins</span><span>2 on</span></summary>
<div class="plugrow"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Hex swatch</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable hex-swatch"></span></div>
<div class="plugrow"><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span class="plugname">Morning agenda</span><span class="plugswitch" aria-label="Enable morning-agenda"></span></div>
</details>
<details class="pluggroup"><summary><span class="plugchev">▶</span><span>Server</span><span>laptop</span></summary></details>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <Fragment set:html={pitch} />
      </div>
      <pre class="tree" aria-label="A plugin in your directory: a folder holding a README, the server half and the browser half">my-notes/
├── plugins/
│   └── hex-swatch/
│       ├── README.md     <i>what it does, for people</i>
│       ├── server.ts     <i>what runs on the server</i>
│       └── browser.tsx   <i>what draws in the page</i>
├── _olai/
│   └── Settings.olai     <i>hex-swatch: on, approved</i>
├── colours.olai
└── kitchen.olai</pre>
    </div>
    <details class="tablewrap allplugins">
      <summary>Every plugin olai ships, and what each one does</summary>
      {plugins.groups.map((group) => (
        <>
          <h3>{group.title}</h3>
          <table class="plug">
            <tbody>
              {group.links.map((link) => (
                <tr><td><a href={link.href}>{link.id.slice("plugins/".length)}</a></td><td set:html={link.summary} /></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </>
      ))}
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="commit">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Git records your edits</h2>
    <p class="lead">Every edit is written to disk at once. Commit from the panel
    when you are ready, or turn on Auto-commit and olai makes one commit after
    fifteen quiet seconds.</p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <pre><code>┌─ Changes ─────────────────────────────────┐
│ olai: Outlines as a collection done       │
│   · chat agent · 12m ago · 1a2b3c4        │
│                                           │
│ OUTLINES ─────────────────────────────    │
│ ☑ roadmap.olai                            │
│   ✓  Outlines as a collection    done     │
│   ✎  Notes: one state, same line  note    │
│   +  Kolu integration: auto-…    created  │
│                                           │
│ OTHER FILES ──────────────────────────    │
│ ☑ README.md                    modified   │
│ ☐ notes/scratch.md            untracked   │
│                                           │
│ 2 commits not on origin/master   [ Push ] │
│         [ Commit 3 changes · 1 file ]     │
└───────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Commit messages start with olai, so the trail is easy to find.
        The rest is in the
        <a href="/docs/git/">git docs</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="try">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Run olai on a Mac or a Linux computer</h2>
    <p class="lead">olai is free, and you do not create an account. You need
    these things to run it today.</p>
    <div class="try">
      <div>
        <ul>
          <li>A Mac or a Linux computer. olai does not run on Windows.</li>
          <li>A terminal.</li>
          <li><a href="https://nixos.org/download/">Nix</a>, a free program that downloads olai and runs it.</li>
          <li>An account with Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Pi, or Oh My Pi, if you want an agent.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="next"><a class="go" href="/docs/start/">Set up olai and write your first line</a></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>This command starts olai on the directory <code>~/notes</code>.</p>
        <pre class="run" id="install" title="click to copy"><code>nix run github:juspay/olai -- web ~/notes</code></pre>
        <p class="caption">The Start page has every step, with the two commands that come before this one.</p>
        <p class="caption">olai has no installer for people who do not use a terminal, and no hosted version. A new olai release can break things. Keep your notes in git, as the Start page shows.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap"><Fragment set:html={notes} /></div>

</main>

<script is:inline>
  const install = document.getElementById("install");
  if (install) {
    install.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const text = install.textContent.replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim();
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        install.title = "copied";
      } catch {
        install.title = "select and copy";
      }
    });
  }

  document.querySelectorAll(".chip").forEach((chip) => {
    chip.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const name = chip.getAttribute("data-theme");
      if (!name) return;
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", name);
      document.querySelectorAll(".chip").forEach((other) => {
        other.classList.toggle("on", other === chip);
      });
    });
